r values fixed) and not for values. That trust is not manufactured, and that the gate gains nothing, are refuted for in range as the account states it, and for an adviser whose aim she knows when her evaluation is a verdict; they hold when nothing the adviser does to her depends on its aim, which is close to the class-level transparency the workspace's Lean already asks. A departure of small probability costs the gated score a fixed amount. The verdicts follow the allowed set a case is given: nineteen of twenty-one in-range failures become legitimate once she allows for every aim, the other two being the two whose source she cannot represent. A threat fails no clause. Fifty-four of fifty-five banked predictions match, which is fit. Nothing registered; every component open or a living note.<br>MIXED — of nine statements about the account, four are refuted and five hold on a stated domain, each as a fact about one formalization. The constraints do not fix purposes in it: in a class of 3,000 candidates over a three-part chain eight are admissible, no two classifying the adviser's actions alike, and a candidate whose goal is whatever she does is excluded only by a condition no extensional test captures (fifteen are admissible without it). Read pairwise, never opposed excludes all eight, and leaves two once the situations where her own judging part reverses a right belief are not counted usual. A lie widens no gap where she was already wrong, and none under four of the eight where it concerns a matter nothing reads. The four kinds are not exclusive, and only the step from serving to not serving survives redescription. That every bad change in what she cares about widens a gap holds in the one scene enumerated, close to by construction; her goal can fall through her parts' coordination with no gap widened. A legitimacy predicate built from gaps has the shapes of the post's scoring and decision, depends on the comparison action (27, 33, 46 or 38 of 57 renderings convicted)